{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788378921610712001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"endowed-upset-scaup","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":8,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"0a0191d7c51fb0b0b57121075cb5abc691fe1016d2190cdc57579848fb67ac32","event_uuid":"67e5aff6-5925-401c-9a62-16d0b318e95d","position":{"commit_sha":"c52797cfe05e479c14ccd05f5b08989ca1438eea","position":"1788374862839289515-67e5aff6-5925-401c-9a62-16d0b318e95d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"df69289e9097018078e078a39bdb69d8c99d519b95cca09adc31966ea00e7540","event_uuid":"8f290556-ba3b-4fb8-ba8b-f7b4c30ee021","position":{"commit_sha":"1838f46ea0a6d0de101f7c16892ccb09345a55fd","position":"1788374907974680084-8f290556-ba3b-4fb8-ba8b-f7b4c30ee021"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"cb80fa9eae13c49466b58cf38934aa643fee35b8e80d64e83ff31d323e92f875","event_uuid":"d8f241ea-5221-4515-8be6-88339f7fa9a0","position":{"commit_sha":"950a5611a4e68c55b1596b1b21cbd4ae53e46d0b","position":"1788375087860455350-d8f241ea-5221-4515-8be6-88339f7fa9a0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"49dd1ae496fcf91db8144327796b790bd62f36e2f82e1d69d5332bb09ef2a612","event_uuid":"4f0d1cee-2bf2-4a98-af81-ff3106f4ebc0","position":{"commit_sha":"5088894bf985acfd52309d4289cc214c55806fd8","position":"1788375124625037517-4f0d1cee-2bf2-4a98-af81-ff3106f4ebc0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"23d2a625340f5b6f38d4e6ea941ddad6614b4a00666250687b5f220e93b05983","event_uuid":"cdaa66ce-1c71-441e-8198-cfbd78001a33","position":{"commit_sha":"f23269555e5ebac7f4cb13a734b37a102efe466c","position":"1788375230576891415-cdaa66ce-1c71-441e-8198-cfbd78001a33"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"cca292cd9e465c66d1819aeec35d0ee1175f9172ba3dc7cf9acfbe8fd49342ab","event_uuid":"cb427de5-c909-4271-a40e-f7a6d3056882","position":{"commit_sha":"4d3842045eb5d6b99fd98bcc72a0c50758364f4c","position":"1788375507950534171-cb427de5-c909-4271-a40e-f7a6d3056882"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9f20bd8a06cccfae67044b6615948d30cc39aa70d1d97ea63642dc309ba6ae60","event_uuid":"00b7600c-388e-4daa-b826-6df57c8274ef","position":{"commit_sha":"5ce92d15793a7ede4439aa336b785107f38c7833","position":"1788375536272509090-00b7600c-388e-4daa-b826-6df57c8274ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fd07fb7994b6a8d87e126260f8221080449b0e5c42a5a54dc1e44d7fae998ee5","event_uuid":"4fe1eb3b-7176-46b0-b631-d334ba093d84","position":{"commit_sha":"d7d8b4bac40a57efd7434b2e0ae5f88472745910","position":"1788376292927408159-4fe1eb3b-7176-46b0-b631-d334ba093d84"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788374862839289515,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4f0d1cee-2bf2-4a98-af81-ff3106f4ebc0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd"},{"link_uuid":"cb427de5-c909-4271-a40e-f7a6d3056882","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3e92-b7f4-dede-4c17"}],"description":"# Bounded disk-ceiling architecture for the Gerrit host\n\n## Context\nDiscovered from `cyclopean-bloodshot-hoatzin` (`3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd`), the 2026-09-02 root-volume outage that took Gerrit offline for ~5h. Defect 2 from that incident (disk alarms self-cleared when metrics stopped because `treat_missing_data=notBreaching`) stays on that bug and was fixed/landed/applied live. This epic is Defect 1: root-volume consumers grow without a bounded ceiling.\n\nOperator-approved design — firm standing intent, do not re-litigate:\n\n1. **Option A: per-accumulator HARD SIZE CAPS via native GC/retention.** Each disk consumer gets a hard upper bound enforced by its own native garbage-collection or retention mechanism. Consumers to cap: Docker overlay2/image layers + build cache (BuildKit/Docker GC policy with `maxUsedSpace` / `--keep-storage` style limits), `/var/tmp` (tmpfiles cleanup plus a real size/quota mechanism where required), journald (`SystemMaxUse`), and writable container layers (runtime storage quota where supportable, or bounded periodic reaping of exited containers). **Hard operator constraint:** every capped generator must have its own CloudWatch alarm at/near its cap, so capacity visibility names the saturated generator rather than only saying \"root disk high\".\n2. **Option C: separate EBS volume for code-review scratch.** Gate scratch/clones/snapshots currently share root via system temp (e.g. `/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots`). Move this workload to a dedicated, independently sized/quota'd gp3 EBS volume mounted at a documented path, and configure gate temp/snapshot code so review work can never fill the OS/root disk.\n3. **Sibling carried from cyclopean AC5:** fold in `scowlful-bovine-dragonfly` (`3e92-b7f4-dede-4c17`), the `/var/gerrit` data-volume prevention/runbook task, by linking it into this epic rather than duplicating it.\n\nThe root volume was grown 30→60 GiB during recovery and should stay 60 GiB, but that is headroom only, not the fix: an unbounded generator can fill 60 GiB as readily as 30 GiB.\n\n## Scope\nThis epic scaffolds and later implements the approved architecture only. Defect 2 alarm-missing-data remediation remains on `cyclopean-bloodshot-hoatzin`. The full ADR draft is captured in child S0 to keep this epic below the 8,000-character plan-review admission cap; no ADR file is created by this scaffold-only work.\n\n## Research grounding\n- Current Terraform owns a single EC2 host plus `/var/gerrit` data EBS volume: `infra/terraform/main.tf:27-35`, `:42-64`, `:83-87`; size variables are in `infra/terraform/variables.tf:13-23`.\n- `infra/terraform/user_data.sh:20-70` is the existing attach/mount pattern: resolve Nitro NVMe device by EBS volume id, format idempotently, mount by UUID in `/etc/fstab`.\n- `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh:21-31` and `:82-99` create Docker bind volumes under `/var/gerrit/site`; current review-bot compose has no tmp/scratch mount and notes `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` is unset (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:233-245`).\n- Snapshot store and clone locations: `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:149-163` uses `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` else `tempfile.gettempdir()` and creates `rebar-gate-snapshots`; `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:381` clones into `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")`; `src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py:69` checks free space on `tempfile.gettempdir()`.\n- Observability/alarm seams: `infra/scripts/observability.sh:72-90` publishes current data/root disk metrics; root alarm is `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:207-239`; data alarm is `infra/terraform/monitoring.tf:217-244`.\n- Existing reactive reclaimers are in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:132-140`, `:367-384`, and `:410-445`; runbook coverage is `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:494-606` and provisioning order is `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md:98-138`.\n- Prior incident tickets found: `resting-feudalist-screamer` (`2731`), `masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle` (`3a52`), `besotted-witty-murrelet` (`e4f3`), `preodorous-temporary-piglet` (`3cef`), current `cyclopean-bloodshot-hoatzin` (`3276`), plus data-volume sibling `wakeful-ordinary-chicken` (`5a05`).\n\n## ADR draft location\nS0 `livid-blondish-shearwater` contains the full ADR draft to land later as `docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md` plus `docs/adr/.numbers/0110`, matching `docs/adr/README.md` and recent ADR format. Related accepted ADRs to cite: ADR 0005, ADR 0012, ADR 0069/0077, and ADR 0104.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ADR 0110 is finalized and landed in `docs/adr/` with number marker and index update if required by repo convention.\n- [ ] Dedicated gate-scratch EBS volume exists, is mounted at a documented path, is used by gate snapshots and review clone tempdirs, and has its own disk alarm.\n- [ ] Each named root accumulator has an enforced cap and its own CloudWatch alarm at/near cap.\n- [ ] Existing root/data disk alarms remain present; the cyclopean missing-data fix is not regressed.\n- [ ] `scowlful-bovine-dragonfly` is linked as the carried-over `/var/gerrit` sibling and is resolved or explicitly dispositioned before epic close.\n- [ ] Runbooks document steady-state ceilings, per-generator alarms, and emergency remediation.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: implementation is Terraform + host Docker/systemd config + host metrics, with local/scripted validation; it does not depend on any single CI provider trigger.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md","reason":"ADR to record the approved disk-ceiling architecture."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0110","reason":"ADR number marker required by docs/adr convention."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"ADR index/category entry if repository convention requires regeneration."},{"path":"infra/terraform/main.tf","reason":"Epic implementation will add a gate-scratch EBS volume and attachments."},{"path":"infra/terraform/variables.tf","reason":"Epic implementation will add size/cap/mount variables."},{"path":"infra/terraform/user_data.sh","reason":"Epic implementation will mount new scratch volume and install host ceiling config."},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf","reason":"Epic implementation will add per-generator CloudWatch alarms near current root-disk alarm area."},{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Epic implementation will publish per-generator disk saturation metrics."},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Epic implementation will replace/tighten Docker reactive pruning with cap-aware behavior."},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"Epic implementation will point review-bot gate temp/snapshot paths at scratch volume."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"Epic implementation will update disk ceiling/recovery runbook."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md","reason":"Epic implementation will update fresh-provision/restore steps for scratch volume."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","3e92-b7f4-dede-4c17"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["infra","gerrit","disk-ceiling","operator-approved"],"ticket_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Bounded disk-ceiling architecture for the Gerrit host","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"ADR and ticket hierarchy are complete before epic close."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py tests/scripts/test_observability_disk_pressure.py","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"Infra tests for alarms/observability/prune behavior pass across the epic changes."},{"command":"terraform -chdir=infra/terraform validate","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"Terraform syntax remains valid."}]},"source_event_uuids":["67e5aff6-5925-401c-9a62-16d0b318e95d","8f290556-ba3b-4fb8-ba8b-f7b4c30ee021","d8f241ea-5221-4515-8be6-88339f7fa9a0","4f0d1cee-2bf2-4a98-af81-ff3106f4ebc0","cdaa66ce-1c71-441e-8198-cfbd78001a33","cb427de5-c909-4271-a40e-f7a6d3056882","00b7600c-388e-4daa-b826-6df57c8274ef","4fe1eb3b-7176-46b0-b631-d334ba093d84"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788378921610712001,"uuid":"624c4d45-cb65-4e50-8ea2-92636e154f22"}